krita: allow skipping the macOS Finder integration plugins

krita/integration builds the Spotlight importer and the Quick Look
thumbnailer/preview with `xcodebuild archive`. That needs a full Xcode
installation and an Xcode project archive step, which neither the Nix
sandbox nor nixpkgs' xcbuild provides, so the target fails the whole
build. These plugins only add Finder integration, so let the package
skip them.

--- a/krita/integration/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/krita/integration/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-if (APPLE)
+if (APPLE AND NOT KRITA_SKIP_MACOS_INTEGRATION)
 project(kritaintegration)
 
 if (NOT MACOS_UNIVERSAL)
